@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`

-- hvac-simplex-scenarios.l4 -- the scenarios of the SimpLEX test table and its worked example,
-- as named values, so that the green tests and the red tests refer to the same thing.
--
-- Source: Figure 4 of Schwartz, Bar-Siman-Tov & Gelbard (2025), the panel
-- "תרחישי בדיקה לבחינות מקצועיות" (test scenarios for professional exams), read by eye
-- from a low-resolution crop of the screenshot (inputs/fig4-simplex-screenshot.png).
-- Rows 5 to 8 of the table, as printed (columns: scenario | expected outcome | reference):
--
--   5  הרשמה לבחינה עיונית            הרשמה מאושרת    תקנה 2(א)
--   6  הרשמה לבחינה מעשית             הרשמה מאושרת    תקנה 2(ב)
--   7  ערעור עם תשלום (40 ש"ח)         הערעור נבדק     תקנה 2(ג)
--   8  הרשמה לבחינה ללא תשלום          השעיית שירות    תקנה 4
--
-- The worked example beneath it ("תרחיש לדוגמה"):
--   תרחיש: מועמד נרשם לבחינה עיונית אבל לא משלם את האגרה.
--   סעיף 9(א): מחייב מעבר בחינה.      (green tick)
--   תקנה 4: אוסרת רישום ללא תשלום.    (red cross)
--   תוצאה: הרשמה נדחית – חובה להשלים תשלום.
--
-- Rows 7 and 8 do not say which exam they concern, and row 5 and 6 do not say whether the
-- fee was paid; "registration approved" in rows 5 and 6 is read as "registration with the
-- fee paid in full" (the panel's own row 8 is the unpaid case).  Rows 7 and 8 are run for
-- both exams (fork F-T1).  The panel has a SECOND section below this one, "תרחישי בדיקה
-- לעדכוני אגרות ומדד" (relevant: Law s 59, regulations 3(א)-(ב)); the screenshot cuts it off
-- after its header row, so none of its scenarios is known and none is transcribed.

--  the request, the exam, the fee paid in full
`row 5: registration for a theory exam`               MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `registration for an exam`,        `Theory exam`,    TRUE
`row 6: registration for a practical exam`            MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `registration for an exam`,        `Practical exam`, TRUE
`row 7: an appeal with payment, on a theory exam`     MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `an appeal against an exam score`, `Theory exam`,    TRUE
`row 7: an appeal with payment, on a practical exam`  MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `an appeal against an exam score`, `Practical exam`, TRUE
`row 8: registration for a theory exam without payment`    MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `registration for an exam`,   `Theory exam`,    FALSE
`row 8: registration for a practical exam without payment` MEANS `SimpLEX scenario` OF `registration for an exam`,   `Practical exam`, FALSE

-- The worked example: a candidate registers for a theory exam and does not pay.
`the worked example` MEANS `row 8: registration for a theory exam without payment`
